WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.549 --> 00:00:08.559
I want to start today by trying at least to
run some interference and introduce some facts

00:00:08.559 --> 00:00:10.910
into the wild.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:14.160
Disinformation really is what it is, disinformation
and ignorance and talking points that are

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:20.249
spreading about crime in the United States,
because there are actually some, I believe,

00:00:20.249 --> 00:00:24.890
well-intentioned people, including people
on the left, who are falling for some of these

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:30.480
talking points and are ending up in places
where they certainly shouldn't be.

00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:34.200
And one of the things that can become difficult,
particularly right now, is that one of the

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:40.070
techniques that the right uses is to continually,
you could say, move the goalposts.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:44.390
You can say to get Gallup, which is just to
throw a whole bunch of stuff out, making it

00:00:44.390 --> 00:00:46.030
hard to refute each piece.

00:00:46.030 --> 00:00:50.809
But if you did refute each piece, you would
realize there's really nothing there.

00:00:50.809 --> 00:00:56.130
And the area where I'm going to focus on today's
crime, because in the wake of the George Floyd

00:00:56.130 --> 00:01:02.629
protests, in the context of calls from some
on the left to either defund or abolish the

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:07.790
police in a broader context, were most most
of the left wants to reform.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:14.260
You're starting to hear all of these subsequent
steps being taken to get to Joe Biden will

00:01:14.260 --> 00:01:18.170
cancel all police and your kids will be killed
as a result of it.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:19.170
Right.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:20.230
Like, that's where they want to end up.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:22.290
There's all these intermediate steps.

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.770
And one of those steps is crime is going up.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:27.130
There's more crime right now.

00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:32.290
And they talk about this in the context of
Portland and Chicago, often by playing, you

00:01:32.290 --> 00:01:35.220
know, 30 second clips of this or that thing
happening.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:38.800
So we absolutely have to go step by step.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:44.950
So first and foremost, if we're going to talk
about whether defunding police once Joe Biden

00:01:44.950 --> 00:01:49.190
does, it will do X or Y to rising crime rates.

00:01:49.190 --> 00:01:52.280
We've got to figure out, is that actually
Joe Biden's plan?

00:01:52.280 --> 00:01:55.920
Would such plans, if they existed, actually
be successful?

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:58.010
But most importantly, is crime going up right
now?

00:01:58.010 --> 00:02:01.990
And crime rates in the United States on a
year to year basis have been declining.

00:02:01.990 --> 00:02:07.600
That is the first fact we have to introduce
here, because the entire conversation stems

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:12.730
from that, despite the fact that we have more
and more people living in the United States

00:02:12.730 --> 00:02:14.530
over time.

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:19.490
Actual crime rates for things like violent
crime, robbery, property crimes.

00:02:19.490 --> 00:02:22.540
It has all been declining on a per household
basis.

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:27.880
When you survey people and you ask them, do
you think crime has increased in the United

00:02:27.880 --> 00:02:30.310
States from last year?

00:02:30.310 --> 00:02:35.090
Almost every year, more than 50 percent of
the people in the United States believe that,

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:36.750
yes, crime has actually gone up.

00:02:36.750 --> 00:02:41.120
So crime has been going down since the early
90s.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:44.450
People mostly believe crime has been going
up OK.

00:02:44.450 --> 00:02:46.090
That's step one.

00:02:46.090 --> 00:02:52.770
Now, there are a whole bunch of other details
and complications that warrant some more exploration.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.460
So let's do a couple of them before we move
on.

00:02:55.460 --> 00:03:00.790
For example, some types of crime might be
up one year, even in the midst of a downward

00:03:00.790 --> 00:03:06.650
trend or some types of crime might be up one
year even when other types of crime are down.

00:03:06.650 --> 00:03:13.940
So as an example, in 2020, murder is up slightly,
but a whole bunch of other crimes are down.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:17.470
And over time, all of these types of violent
crime are down.

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:23.959
So you would have to decide, can I really
make any relevant observation in one year

00:03:23.959 --> 00:03:30.209
about, well, murders up, but rape and robbery
or down and arson is up.

00:03:30.209 --> 00:03:32.940
But burglary and sexual assault or whatever.

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:33.940
Right.

00:03:33.940 --> 00:03:40.110
So overall, crime rates have been declining
for a long time and they continue to decline.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:43.400
It's also important to remember that not all
crimes are reported to police.

00:03:43.400 --> 00:03:48.531
So any time we're looking at something that
depends on reporting to an authority, you

00:03:48.531 --> 00:03:53.860
have to consider that the records may not
reflect reality at equal rates.

00:03:53.860 --> 00:03:57.130
So as an example, which many on the right
don't like.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:00.220
Sexual assault is notoriously under reported.

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.601
However, that doesn't really fit into their
narrative.

00:04:02.601 --> 00:04:05.930
If they want to make it seem as though crime
in general is underreported, you really have

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.930
to start with sexual assault, which they don't
seem particularly willing to do.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:15.410
Then you have other crimes, crimes like vandalism
and public intoxication, which arguably should

00:04:15.410 --> 00:04:21.019
not even really be a crime, which certainly
are visible in that you see graffiti or a

00:04:21.019 --> 00:04:24.460
broken window or whatever the case may be.

00:04:24.460 --> 00:04:29.050
But those are not the serious violent crimes
that were really mostly talking about when

00:04:29.050 --> 00:04:31.610
we talk about how police should be reformed.

00:04:31.610 --> 00:04:37.840
So that gets us to what's going on today since
the George Floyd protests have started.

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:41.020
We've been hearing defund the police.

00:04:41.020 --> 00:04:43.069
We've been hearing abolish the police.

00:04:43.069 --> 00:04:44.469
We've been hearing reform.

00:04:44.469 --> 00:04:47.340
We've been hearing just fund the police blindly.

00:04:47.340 --> 00:04:48.680
Give them as much money as they want.

00:04:48.680 --> 00:04:50.879
We've heard every combination of things.

00:04:50.879 --> 00:04:56.439
The majority of the left, including Joe Biden,
is talking about reform.

00:04:56.439 --> 00:04:58.571
It could include reallocation of funds to.

00:04:58.571 --> 00:05:02.680
Taking funds away maybe for militarization
while increasing funds for training.

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:04.330
As one example.

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:09.029
But it doesn't really matter in terms of the
crime we're seeing now, because remember all

00:05:09.029 --> 00:05:13.610
of the discussions about defunding, abolishing,
restructuring, all that stuff.

00:05:13.610 --> 00:05:14.930
It's in the future.

00:05:14.930 --> 00:05:16.129
It hasn't happened yet.

00:05:16.129 --> 00:05:20.229
And yet still, you have people like Donald
Trump himself and his acolytes tweeting videos

00:05:20.229 --> 00:05:27.229
of things going on now in Portland or Chicago,
saying this is the future of the country.

00:05:27.229 --> 00:05:28.900
If Joe Biden is elected president.

00:05:28.900 --> 00:05:30.229
Hold on a second.

00:05:30.229 --> 00:05:33.319
First of all, that's Trump's America right
now.

00:05:33.319 --> 00:05:38.330
So to say this is what's going on now and
this is what would be happening even more

00:05:38.330 --> 00:05:43.610
under Joe Biden, you then have to see what
is it that Joe Biden would do that would exacerbate

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:44.610
this.

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:45.819
And there actually isn't anything.

00:05:45.819 --> 00:05:52.460
But it also ignores that none of these abolish
or defund things have become a reality.

00:05:52.460 --> 00:05:58.069
So they are arguing we are seeing more crime
in cities because police have been defunded

00:05:58.069 --> 00:05:59.369
by Democrats.

00:05:59.369 --> 00:06:03.960
The reality is crime continues to go down
and nothing has been defunded yet.

00:06:03.960 --> 00:06:09.340
There have been some conversations in certain
places about how might we reduce funding to

00:06:09.340 --> 00:06:11.280
police in some places.

00:06:11.280 --> 00:06:16.030
You know, the Northampton, Massachusetts,
is a place where the show started, where there's

00:06:16.030 --> 00:06:17.759
been this discussion.

00:06:17.759 --> 00:06:22.259
There's been a decrease to the rate at which
police funding will increase.

00:06:22.259 --> 00:06:24.409
If that makes sense.

00:06:24.409 --> 00:06:26.400
But all of this stuff is in the future.

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:34.990
So you certainly can't blame a future, possible
changes to police funding for current increases

00:06:34.990 --> 00:06:39.020
in crime, particularly when there have been
no such increases today.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:41.439
There have been discussions about do we change?

00:06:41.439 --> 00:06:47.599
Who responds to certain types of nine one
one calls when they when they relate to homelessness

00:06:47.599 --> 00:06:49.779
or mental illness as an example.

00:06:49.779 --> 00:06:50.779
OK.

00:06:50.779 --> 00:06:52.069
Those discussions have been had.

00:06:52.069 --> 00:06:55.999
There are some places that have started to
look at making some of those changes, but

00:06:55.999 --> 00:06:59.539
these policies haven't yet been put in place
when it comes to defund or abolish.

00:06:59.539 --> 00:07:03.809
I don't think that they are going to and Joe
Biden certainly doesn't support them.

00:07:03.809 --> 00:07:10.499
So when you look at this broader context,
you do have to ask, why are people falling

00:07:10.499 --> 00:07:13.180
for the idea that crime is up?

00:07:13.180 --> 00:07:18.279
And this actually takes me back to my days
as an undergrad at the University of Massachusetts

00:07:18.279 --> 00:07:24.669
AMR's, where Michael Morgan, who's been a
guest on this program, studied this extensively.

00:07:24.669 --> 00:07:26.569
Erica Ashar also studied this.

00:07:26.569 --> 00:07:29.289
And both of those interviews are on the YouTube
channel.

00:07:29.289 --> 00:07:32.539
There's often this assumption and we see it
after mass shootings.

00:07:32.539 --> 00:07:37.759
We see it after a lot of things that violence
in the media and in popular culture, in movies

00:07:37.759 --> 00:07:42.099
and video games makes people act violently
in the real world.

00:07:42.099 --> 00:07:45.580
Now, by and large, that doesn't seem to be
true.

00:07:45.580 --> 00:07:48.240
It if you look at the scholarship on this.

00:07:48.240 --> 00:07:53.749
It's certainly possible that people already
predisposed to be violent in the real world

00:07:53.749 --> 00:07:59.979
might be triggered to act in a particular
way based on things they consume in violent

00:07:59.979 --> 00:08:00.979
video games or movies.

00:08:00.979 --> 00:08:03.599
But that's a small, small portion of the population.

00:08:03.599 --> 00:08:10.469
By and large, we have not found that violent
video games or watching violent news or whatever

00:08:10.469 --> 00:08:13.529
makes people violent in the new in the real
world.

00:08:13.529 --> 00:08:19.849
However, what does seem to be the case is
that seeing violence on the news and in media

00:08:19.849 --> 00:08:25.879
may make people more afraid, and it makes
people believe that the world is more dangerous

00:08:25.879 --> 00:08:26.879
than it is.

00:08:26.879 --> 00:08:31.309
And in fact, when you look at local news and
you realize, wow, murder is down over the

00:08:31.309 --> 00:08:35.190
last 30 years, all of these violent crimes
are down over the last 30 years.

00:08:35.190 --> 00:08:38.819
But the representation in media is identical
or has even grown because of this.

00:08:38.819 --> 00:08:41.440
If it bleeds, it leads ideology.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:46.410
It makes sense that based on watching news,
people would believe the world is more dangerous

00:08:46.410 --> 00:08:47.410
than it is.

00:08:47.410 --> 00:08:50.650
People would believe there is more crime than
there actually is.

00:08:50.650 --> 00:08:58.360
So what you have right now, in part thanks
to the Trump administration, is this use.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:00.300
It's all based on getting Trump reelected.

00:09:00.300 --> 00:09:03.079
And we're going to deal with that a little
bit more later in the show.

00:09:03.079 --> 00:09:08.300
You have a lot of discussion of very rare
individual incidents that are happening in

00:09:08.300 --> 00:09:10.740
the shadows of mostly peaceful protests.

00:09:10.740 --> 00:09:15.110
But the takeaway we have to remember is that
crime rates have been on the decline since

00:09:15.110 --> 00:09:20.820
the 90s and there certainly has been no defunding
of the police yet, which you could blame for

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:24.339
nonexistent crime increases that they claim
exist.

00:09:24.339 --> 00:09:28.900
Now, one other thing that I think is important
to think about, and that's the war on drugs

00:09:28.900 --> 00:09:30.910
and prison populations.

00:09:30.910 --> 00:09:36.640
Some will say clearly there is more crime
because people are in prison for committing

00:09:36.640 --> 00:09:38.399
crimes more than ever before.

00:09:38.399 --> 00:09:40.380
There are more people in prison right now.

00:09:40.380 --> 00:09:43.019
So clearly, there's more crime going on.

00:09:43.019 --> 00:09:45.750
Just because there are more people in prison.

00:09:45.750 --> 00:09:50.209
Doesn't mean that the streets of the United
States are more dangerous from a violent crime

00:09:50.209 --> 00:09:51.430
standpoint.

00:09:51.430 --> 00:09:56.709
If you add things to the list of stuff that
will get you put in prison, you would expect

00:09:56.709 --> 00:09:58.440
that more people are going to end up.

00:09:58.440 --> 00:10:04.260
Prison, if you put in place mandatory minimums
or if judicial discretion is used to sentence

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:06.800
people to longer prison sentences.

00:10:06.800 --> 00:10:14.199
You can see prisons more full, even if violent
crime is on the decline in general society,

00:10:14.199 --> 00:10:15.199
which it is.

00:10:15.199 --> 00:10:20.610
So it's really important not to fall for that
propaganda because at every level there is

00:10:20.610 --> 00:10:21.710
to go back to the beginning.

00:10:21.710 --> 00:10:27.319
There is a gift, Gallup going on where a whole
bunch of stuff is thrown out.

00:10:27.319 --> 00:10:28.399
Crime is up.

00:10:28.399 --> 00:10:30.160
And it's crime because Paul is.

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:32.160
It's up because police have been defunded.

00:10:32.160 --> 00:10:34.100
And Joe Biden would do more of that.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:35.230
You've got to break it down.

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:36.580
Is crime up?

00:10:36.580 --> 00:10:37.580
No.

00:10:37.580 --> 00:10:41.579
Have police been defunded already in a way
that would even relate to what we're seeing

00:10:41.579 --> 00:10:42.579
right now?

00:10:42.579 --> 00:10:43.579
No.

00:10:43.579 --> 00:10:47.050
Does Joe Biden want to defund the full police
if if he becomes president?

00:10:47.050 --> 00:10:48.050
No.

00:10:48.050 --> 00:10:53.050
Every single one of the premises is wrong
and they count on because they don't have

00:10:53.050 --> 00:10:55.100
the facts on their side side.

00:10:55.100 --> 00:11:00.000
They count on you not knowing the facts or
you not checking the facts and ending up having

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.540
to argue on the merits.

00:11:01.540 --> 00:11:07.060
And when we accept the facts and debate what
should be done, we're missing the fact that

00:11:07.060 --> 00:11:09.060
the premises are all wrong.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:15.720
Hopefully this is useful when we see everything
from Don Junior's tweets to discussions in

00:11:15.720 --> 00:11:19.720
right wing media and on the Internet about
these issues.

00:11:19.720 --> 00:11:22.790
Go and look at whether the premises make sense
and check out.

00:11:22.790 --> 00:11:24.940
In this case, they don't.

00:11:24.940 --> 00:11:29.800
Starting with crime has been on a downward
trend for decades in the United States.

00:11:29.800 --> 00:11:30.800
Let me know what you think.

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:32.750
I'm on Twitter at Deas Pacman.

00:11:32.750 --> 00:11:34.759
We have a lot happening this week.

00:11:34.759 --> 00:11:39.490
This is the month of the 15 year anniversary
of the David Pakman show.

00:11:39.490 --> 00:11:40.490
Can you imagine that?

00:11:40.490 --> 00:11:43.430
And I'll talk to you later on in the month
about what we're going to do.

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:46.019
The exact date is in the second half of the
month.

00:11:46.019 --> 00:11:47.190
But a very, very exciting month.

00:11:47.190 --> 00:12:59.809
We'll take a quick break and be back right
after this.

